WEBVTT

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.090
Can you imagine...

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:16.300
...a life in which you could never
touch the one you love?

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.560
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.980
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.850
His own mother has
distanced herself from him.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.190
His friends have called him a monster.

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:31.360
Even strangers have spoken of him as the
Death incarnate that dwells in the forest.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.030
And yet,

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.240
he doesn't feel the least bit lonely.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.750
"Episode 8: White Snow, Black Clothes"

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.340
A... B...

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.340
...C...

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.340
...E?

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.720
D comes after C.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.100
Aw, this is so hard to remember.
It's giving me a headache.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.140
You've only just started, so...

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.810
Yeah, we're here to give you our support.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.020
Sorry. I want to learn to read
and write as quickly as possible

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.480
so I can surprise Zain.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.320
That's amazing, Cuff!

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.900
You're so smart!

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.320
Speaking of Zain, where is he today?

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.950
He's at the circus.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.530
You sold him to the circus?!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.330
Since we've got nothing better to do,
both of us have started working there.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.960
At the circus, our looks don't matter.
No one will suspect we're witches.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.880
What do you think of that?
Zain's pretty smart, huh?

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.340
Um, well...

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:58.630
As usual, Cuff thinks
pretty highly of Zain...

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.470
Anyway, it's important to learn your ABCs.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.510
So, be sure and study hard, Ms. Cuff.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.930
Okay, I'm counting on you, Teach!

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.560
By the way, what does the
"Ms." in "Ms. Cuff" mean?

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.980
I'm not quite sure.
I just thought it has a nice ring to it.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:13.810
So, he fudges the answer there...

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.780
Good morning, Lord Walter.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.700
Good morning.

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.330
Lookin' cool.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:32.040
You're a regular teen idol.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.590
Viola, you aren't thinking of running
off somewhere again, are you?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.420
It's almost time for lunch.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:40.420
Try to appreciate the trouble I have
to go through placating Mother.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.260
I can't help it.
I've got things to do.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:49.060
Don't tell me you're going to the villa
where our cursed brother lives.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.140
It's none of your business, Dear Brother.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.640
It is too my business.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.560
I shall soon be in the position
of inheriting the family title.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.400
It's my duty as head of the family to know
what my younger sister is thinking.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.490
But you're the secondborn son.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:05.120
If our brother can break his curse, then
naturally he'll be head of the family.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.330
Because he's the firstborn son.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:12.210
How can you be so cruel and say
the words that upset me the most!

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.500
You're overreacting.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.870
All I said was that you're
the secondborn son.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:16.290
There, you said it again!

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:17.840
You said it again!

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:22.050
To begin with, I never have liked him.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.390
The only thing that he's got going for him
is that he was born slightly ahead of me.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.890
I wonder how much longer Mother
is going to pin her hopes on him...

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.180
...when no one knows when
he'll be able to break his curse.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.560
Hey, can I leave as soon
as I've finished my tea?

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.900
--I haven't got a second--
--Secondborn son?!

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.150
--You want to remind me I'm
the secondborn son again?! Huh?!
--Jeez, he's such a pain in the neck!

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.150
All right, fair enough.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.450
So, how long does it take
to get to the villa from here?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.700
Hmm, about two hours, I guess.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.830
You tripped up there, Viola!

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.450
You were planning on going
to the villa, after all!

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:54.500
But the "two" in "two hours"...

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.040
...reminds me of being the
secondborn son, and I can't stand it!

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:59.880
It was the death of him.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.460
Why?

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:03.880
Why are you going to see him?

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.720
Why do you have a soft spot for him?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.140
Why not me?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.180
Don't you think I'd make a better
head of the family than he would?

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.140
You're acting way too desperate,
and it scares me.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:15.190
I'm not particularly planning
on taking his side or yours.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.980
Don't say that! Pick me!

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.070
Anyway, I'm going now.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.070
Don't tell Mother I've
been going to the villa.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.200
Well, I can't make you any promises.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.990
You're only the secondborn son,
after all...

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.670
Forgive me for being late.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.550
Viola said she's going
to a friend's house.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.920
I see.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.380
One of these days, I'll show you.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:49.300
That I'm better than him.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:52.310
And that I'm worthy of being
the head of this family.

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.600
Yoo-hoo!

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.850
Dearest Brother!

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.140
Little Miss Viola's here!

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:02.360
And who might you be?

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.610
I'm Cuff.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.690
I'm a circus performer.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.110
A circus performer?

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.360
Where are the people that live here?

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.660
I have no idea. You might as
well make yourself at home.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.410
Uh-oh, there's something
fishy about her.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:14.370
Did she come in unannounced?

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.950
Well, technically I did too, so...

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.790
This looks like Zain.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.210
A shiny, gold Zain.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.710
She's smiling.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.630
Maybe she's a burglar?

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.880
If she is, then I've got
to do something...

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.340
And if I do, then Rob might reward me
by stroking my hair or something!

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.760
I'm up against just one girl.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.810
With a Viola tackle, even I could...

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.480
Hai-yahh!

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.060
Hers are big and soft, too!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.400
What are you talking about?

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.940
Mother is as flat as a board,

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:50.280
so I probably will be, too...

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.620
She attacked me, and she's
the one taking damage?

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.330
She's just a child.
She probably wants to play.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.330
Come on, don't cry. Can you stand up?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.040
Here's my chance!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.670
I've got you now!

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.010
Knock it off! Let go of me!

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:11.970
No way!

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:16.430
--There, there. What an adorable child!
--Absolutely not! Absolutely, positively not!

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:25.570
Now, I'd rather not do this, but I'm going
to just sit here so you can't move.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.820
Okay. You mind if I go to sleep?

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.820
How can you act so relaxed?!

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.240
A little while ago you shouted out,
"Dearest Brother," or something.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.910
Uh, uh-huh. What about it?

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:36.240
You and your brother are a lot alike.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.660
What?!

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.330
Wait a sec, you know my brother?

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:42.670
Don't lump me together
with a Gloomy Gus like him!

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:44.460
But he's a good guy.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.840
Um, well, I guess he is... a little.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.970
Do you like him?

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:56.970
Huh? Uh, well, um...

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.260
Sorry to keep you waiting, Cuff.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.770
It took us longer than we
thought to catch the cat...

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.310
R-R-R-Rob?

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:05.400
Viola, I see you're here, too...

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.730
Sorry, we'll come back later.

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:10.990
No! This is not what you think! Rob!

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:15.320
I simply can't marry anyone but Rob!

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:17.370
What the heck are you going on about?

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:21.910
I had you pegged as a burglar,

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.370
but it turns out you're
a friend of my brother's.

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:28.250
I didn't know Gloomy Guses had friends.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.630
Hey, no skin off my back.
They were the words of a child, after all.

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:32.550
I am not a child!

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.430
I'm a respectable lady!

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:35.430
Hmm?

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.640
Lady Viola,

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.140
excuse me for a second.

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.230
A speck of dust was ruining
your otherwise beautiful hair.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.690
Th-Thanks, Rob.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:52.610
My wish came true!

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:56.070
Lady Viola's such a charming girl.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:09:00.080
Sometimes I get the feeling
you do these things on purpose...

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:11.960
It's snowing pretty heavily.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.720
Well, we did have a lot
of clear days lately.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.090
I'm glad for nights like these. It's easy
for me to invite you to a cup of tea.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.980
I'm just a beginner, so go
easy on me, please.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:27.400
And you aren't allowed to use
your feminine wiles on me!

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.400
Look out, Alice.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.400
If you take your eyes off the board,
I might just move the pieces around.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.990
All right.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.990
If I lose, I'll strip like we promised.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.450
We never made any promises like that! And
besides, you've already started stripping!

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.250
On snowstormy nights,

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:52.500
I remember the time I first arrived here.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:21.370
I'm coming in, Your Grace.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:24.040
I see you've made a mess
of your room again.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.000
And you haven't even
turned on the lights...

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.370
I don't want to hear any of your lectures.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:31.330
If you're through, then leave me at once.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:35.210
Today I brought someone
I'd like you to meet, Your Grace.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.670
Please, come in.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.800
It's been ages since I last saw you.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:45.140
I'm Alice Lendrott. I shall work here
as your maid starting today.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:47.680
"I-It's been ages"...?

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.100
Who are you?!
I don't know the likes of you!

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.980
Rob! Who told you that
you could hire a maid?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.440
I have the permission of
the lady of the house.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:01.610
And I believe you and Alice were good
friends when you were little, Your Grace.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:05.700
Oh, I have no recollection of that.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.870
I hate my childhood days!
I don't want to be reminded of them!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.080
Go home at once.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.710
There's no place for you in this mansion.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:23.090
I have never forgotten you, Your Grace.
Not even for a single day.

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:29.270
After my mother died,
I was left in my aunt's care.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:32.230
Being able to meet you again in this
way... It's a dream come true, Your Grace.

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:33.520
Don't come near me.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.770
If I touch you, I'll kill you.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.440
I'm aware of that.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:40.900
A-Anyway, I won't allow you to work here.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.200
Go back to your aunt's home
or wherever you came from!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.540
Well, now that we have His Grace's
blessing, let's pick out your room, Alice.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.500
I haven't given you my blessing!

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.500
You sure have some selective hearing!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:57.590
You may have a grown-up body,

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.960
but your eyes haven't changed a bit.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.930
They still have that
gentle look, Your Grace.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:09.850
Who the heck does she think she is?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.690
Just leave me alone. I'm begging you.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.700
I'll die alone and on my own.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:25.820
Hmm?

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.460
Are you sure you'd like to stay in there?

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:36.290
It's an old storage shed
in need of repair.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:39.050
Yes, I feel more comfortable
in cramped quarters.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.170
You must have been
quite shocked back there.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:46.300
He's an adolescent boy, you see,
and lately he acts like that all the time.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:48.470
Well, it doesn't bother me at all.

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:50.600
Well, that's a relief.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.640
Let me say again,
it's a pleasure to have you here.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.890
The pleasure is mine.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.230
I'll work as hard as I can.

00:12:57.230 --> 00:13:02.610
Well, I must say you really do
take after your mother, Alice.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:03.990
People often tell me that.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:08.700
Hey! You're still here?!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.250
What's with the mourning dress...

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:14.750
Don't tell me that's your maid uniform!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:15.790
Yes, it is.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.670
Your Grace, that hat...

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.750
...looks really good on you.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:23.510
Th-This old thing? It was just lying
around, so I decided to put it on.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.800
But that's beside the point!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:29.930
That maid uniform is too showy!
It's grounds for immediate dismissal!

00:13:29.930 --> 00:13:32.720
Is it really too showy?

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.810
Around the bust, perhaps?

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:38.610
As in, you can't get them off your mind,
and you want to give them a touch?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:42.320
Yesterday you told me you knew
about my curse, didn't you?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.400
Of course I know about it.

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.690
If so, then why?

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:46.360
Who the heck do you think you are?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.110
I'm Alice.

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:51.530
I didn't ask you to tell me your name.

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.450
I hate you!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:54.910
I hate you so much!

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.460
Don't follow me!

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:10.680
It's pointless playing the piano now...

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.930
So, this is where you've been, Your Grace.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.430
I've brought you your dinner.

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:19.270
Won't you try eating just a little bit?

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.440
I-I don't want any.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:24.190
I told you, didn't I? I'm not going to eat
anything until you leave this place.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:27.280
Do you not like me?

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.570
No, I don't!

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.070
I bet you're laughing
at me inside your mind.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:35.200
Because I'm an ugly grouch
and cursed on top of that.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:38.750
I'm a person who's better off dead.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.080
You say you want to be of some use to me.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:44.000
But you're actually an egotist
who only wants to glorify herself.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:49.260
Your words are so poetic, Your Grace.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:56.220
At any rate, I'll leave your dinner here,
so you can eat it if you feel like it.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:05.900
I see you're also wearing gloves today.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:07.690
They look very nice on you.

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.950
After your aunt took you in...

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:20.210
...you went through a great deal
of hardship. I suspected as much.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:21.880
I had my share of hardship.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.130
It's not as though my
aunt's family was well off.

00:15:25.130 --> 00:15:29.340
But compared to His Grace,
my life's been...

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.510
Alice! Could you come
with me for a minute?

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.640
What's with that look on your face?

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:38.270
It's just that I was glad to hear
you call me by my name.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.690
Huh?! A-Anyway, come with me!

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.150
My, what a lovely room!

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:50.610
Are you being sarcastic?

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:53.370
I want you to clean this up in three days.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.120
If you can't, then you're fired.

00:15:56.740 --> 00:15:58.660
And don't ask Rob for any help, either.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:00.160
So, it's settled then.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:01.250
Good luck.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.380
I'll do my best!

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.810
Give me your hand.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.980
I'll take you to your room.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.060
You get sick a lot, don't you?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:25.230
You shouldn't be going outside then.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.110
Your hand's so warm!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:43.710
Wow!

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:47.790
How's this?

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:50.130
Don't tell me you did
all this in one night?!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.010
Yes, I did.

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:54.840
Thinking that I could be of use to
you really fired me up, Your Grace.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:03.890
When I told you to leave, I did it
for your own good as well.

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:08.570
There must something more
meaningful for you to do...

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.900
...than taking care of a wretch like me.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:18.950
I have nowhere else to go, Your Grace,
and I'd like to be by your side.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:26.290
Do you still not want
to remember who I am?

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:32.630
I'll wait until you remember
me, Your Grace.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:33.840
Suit yourself.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:40.510
How long are you going to sit there?

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:43.600
Until your tears subside, Your Grace.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.110
It's gotten chilly in here.

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.240
Shall I make us some more tea?

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.780
No, that's all right.

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:00.370
I'd rather you stay here...

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.200
You're not leaving,

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.700
so I'm leaving!

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.420
I'm cold to the touch.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.720
My feet ache so much.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.970
I don't know which way
the mansion is anymore.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:20.680
This is so hard.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:22.760
I'm sad,

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:24.720
lonely, and miserable.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:31.060
"No one shall love you,
and you shall love no one."

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:34.110
"You shall live a life of misery."

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.110
Are you happy now, witch?

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.160
This is all your fault.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.620
I wish...

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.040
...I had the chance to love someone.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:56.550
I thought I was a goner there.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.140
Well, maybe I should just die.

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.060
Just resign myself...

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.770
...to my fate.

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:13.820
Ever since I was cursed,
I've lived an unhappy joke of a life.

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:16.940
I yearned for even a single friend.

00:19:16.940 --> 00:19:18.570
Is that asking too much?

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:25.830
I remember now.
That girl's name was Alice, too.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:28.910
Yeah, that's right, that's right!

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.460
I'd hoped I could see her once again...

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.670
...but I'd forgotten about her.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:43.180
To think I'd remember her now, when I'm
about to die and can no longer see her.

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:47.270
Alice...

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:55.110
Your Grace?

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:58.280
Alice?!

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.990
I-I've already made up my mind.
I'm going to die.

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.950
Just leave me be!

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:07.910
First off, you can't mind
your own business--

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:09.950
Hey, what are you--?!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:14.000
Why? Why are you throwing your life away?

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.790
Why don't you cool off a bit?

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.250
Uh, wait a-- Hey!

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.880
You've got a right
to be happy, Your Grace!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:23.180
I don't care whether you're cursed or not.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:26.050
I'd hate to see you give up along the way.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:31.060
And please consider the feelings
of those you would leave behind!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:36.650
You know, there are people
who care about you!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:40.990
I was a lonely, sickly child
when I was little.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:45.450
Every day I felt like my anxiety and
hopelessness would overwhelm me.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:51.120
Then you came along, Your Grace,
and saved me with your kindness.

00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.370
I have lived to this very day,
and I have you to thank for it.

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:58.340
Please grab onto this,
and I'll help you up.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.090
Take your time, now.

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:06.970
Let's head on back. And...

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:10.140
...let's keep on living. Together.

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.220
Forever.

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:27.660
Good heavens, I'm so glad you're safe!

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:30.240
Alice rescued me.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.450
And I'm sorry I made you worry, Rob.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.000
Not at all.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:38.000
So, are the two of you getting along now?

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.000
Well...

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:44.720
...I think...

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:46.260
Come again?

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:49.180
About Alice...

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:51.140
...I like her, I think...

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.520
Checkmate.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:53.520
Huh?!

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:54.640
How did that happen?!

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:58.190
To be perfectly honest, Your Grace,
since you weren't paying attention,

00:21:58.190 --> 00:22:00.860
I moved the pieces around a bit.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:02.400
It's not fair.

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:04.280
You're so adorable, and it's not fair.

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:06.820
It's impossible not to like you.

00:22:06.820 --> 00:22:09.240
What are you talking about?

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:10.370
It's not fair.

00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:46.460
"The Duke, Alice,
and the Christmas Eve Vow."
